# HTTP client

## Framework semantics

Outbound HTTP uses `Cake\Http\Client` (or project-wrapped clients registered in DI). Keep credentials in config; keep persistence on Tables — do not put remote IO inside Entities.

## Required behavior

- Prefer CakePHP Http Client or the project’s existing wrapper over ad-hoc curl in new code.
- Timeouts, base URLs, and tokens come from config/`Application::services()`.
- Handle non-2xx explicitly; do not ignore failures.
- Do not call remote APIs from Entity methods by default.

## Anti-patterns

- Hardcoded API keys in client call sites
- Remote IO inside Entities (active-record style)
- Inventing Guzzle service providers when the app standardizes on Cake\Http\Client

## Review checklist

- [ ] Client is configured/injected consistently
- [ ] Errors/timeouts handled
- [ ] Secrets not hardcoded
